{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1092","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1092","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1092\",\"parent_revision\":\"c52685232d9b7e3aa6e7688215001b46a25aae0397cd97d093f1b6f85ce43585\",\"root_revision\":\"c52685232d9b7e3aa6e7688215001b46a25aae0397cd97d093f1b6f85ce43585\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe SAM dispatch loop in implement-feature and complete-implementation cannot make informed reuse decisions without knowing how much context headroom a running or idle teammate has remaining.\\n\\nCurrently there is no mechanism to query a teammate's context usage percentage. The dispatch loop spawns a fresh agent per task regardless of whether an idle same-domain teammate has 60%+ headroom available, wasting the shared-prefix loading cost.\\n\\nWhat is missing: a way to observe context usage for a running teammate before deciding whether to reuse it or spawn fresh.\\n\\nThis is a prerequisite for #1091 (team reuse while context pressure is low). Without a context headroom signal, the reuse condition in the dispatch loop cannot be evaluated.\\n\\nApproaches to investigate:\\n- Whether Claude Code exposes context usage natively via TaskOutput, SendMessage response metadata, or a dedicated tool\\n- A self-report protocol where agents append a structured context-state block to their completion message (e.g., CONTEXT_STATE: {used_tokens: N, capacity: M, headroom_pct: X})\\n- Token estimation from task content size (proxy, not exact)\\n\\nImpact: affects implement-feature progress loop (dispatch step 3), complete-implementation SAM dispatch loop, and any future workflow that benefits from teammate reuse.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-28)\\n\\n### Blocks\\n\\n- #1091 Reuse idle same-domain teammates in SAM dispatch loop\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-28T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **expose teammate context headroom so dispatch loop can make reuse decisions** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-28T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 prerequisite for #1091\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ff324ab7ac269410f280931e5b036ef1e2123ce8dc96d356a089b8bb36d371c0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS8Gmw\"}"}